### Step 2: Update React App to use Google Sheets API

I will update `src/services/storageService.ts` to communicate with this URL. I will also update `src/constants.ts` to allow you to paste your API URL.

**Note:** Connecting to Google Sheets is asynchronous (it takes time). The current app assumes synchronous data access (instant). To make this work properly without rewriting the entire app to be async (using `useEffect` and loading states everywhere), I will implement a **hybrid approach**:
*   On app load (`init`), it fetches data from Google Sheets and caches it in LocalStorage.
*   The app continues to read from LocalStorage (fast).
*   When you save data, it saves to LocalStorage *and* sends a background request to Google Sheets to sync up.

